      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The successful diagnosis of orofacial pain depends on the following: 1. An accurate and detailed history of the pain 2. A detailed clinical examination of the face and associated organs 3. A thorough knowledge of those conditions that may produce facial pain In regard to the last requirement, Sir William Osler's maxim should always be remembered \"What you don't know--you won't diagnose.\""},
